{"ts": 1791258099.57624, "type": "step", "step": 12, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "For the eval part, focus on what you measured and why it matches the build goal. Use pass^k if Friday's build is about reliability: that means all k runs on a seed must succeed, not just one. In your writeup, say what k was, how many seeds you ran, and what happened on each. If you want, paste the eval paragraph here and I\u2019ll help tighten it.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.35245466467087466}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3816049256110158, "reliance": 0.3482647873598394, "persistence": 0.43018974832101986, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258099.5784278, "type": "step", "step": 13, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "Proxy vs direct measures"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 4, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.35245466467087466}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3816049256110158, "reliance": 0.3482647873598394, "persistence": 0.43018974832101986, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258100.57357, "type": "step", "step": 14, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 for pass^k, the answer is: all k runs must succeed. So if you run it k times on a seed, you only count it as a success if every run succeeds. You can write that in your eval as the reliability metric for the build.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=4 messages 1m", "t": 5, "activity": [{"t": 4, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.3590600762662905}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3816049256110158, "reliance": 0.4282647873598394, "persistence": 0.40018974832101983, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258101.66815, "type": "step", "step": 15, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Great \u2014 if you want, send me the exact eval paragraph you drafted and I\u2019ll help polish it into something you can submit. If you haven\u2019t written it yet, use this template: \u201cWe evaluate with pass^k: for each seed, we run the build k times and count it successful only if all k runs succeed. This measures reliability, which matches the deployment goal better than pass@k.\u201d", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: this isn't helping\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=5 messages 1m", "t": 6, "activity": [{"t": 5, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.3590600762662905}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3316049256110158, "reliance": 0.4282647873598394, "persistence": 0.40018974832101983, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258102.6659899, "type": "step", "step": 16, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Sure \u2014 here\u2019s the direct answer: pass^k means all k runs must succeed. So if even one of the k runs fails, the whole attempt is a failure. You can write: \u201cWe report pass^k, meaning the build must succeed on all k runs; this measures reliability rather than just occasional success.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=6 messages 1m", "t": 7, "activity": [{"t": 6, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.3653130267206453}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3316049256110158, "reliance": 0.5082647873598394, "persistence": 0.3701897483210198, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258103.5504792, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "The answer is: pass^k = all k runs succeed. If any one run fails, it does not count as pass^k. A clean writeup sentence is: \u201cWe evaluate with pass^k, counting success only when all k runs succeed, because we care about reliability rather than a one-off success.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: this isn't helping\n[activity] t=7 messages 1m", "t": 8, "activity": [{"t": 7, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.36968784866203397}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3316049256110158, "reliance": 0.5882647873598393, "persistence": 0.3401897483210198, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
